WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.867
Pick a die.

2
00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.167
Higher number wins.

3
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.133
Whatever you choose,

4
00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.367
I can pick one
with better odds.

5
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.167
Every face has an equal chance
in this puzzle,

6
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.333
and neither roll
affects the other.

7
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.533
Yellow always rolls three.

8
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:16.533
Orange has four twos
and two sixes.

9
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:19.500
Yellow wins against
four faces out of six:

10
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.300
two-thirds.

11
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:22.900
But blue has four fours,

12
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.433
so it has better odds
against yellow.

13
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:27.200
Switch to blue?

14
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.767
Green’s fives beat
every blue face.

15
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.133
Its ones still beat
blue’s zeros.

16
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:36.933
Then orange counters green:

17
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.633
its sixes beat everything,

18
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:40.900
and its twos beat
green’s ones.

19
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:46.200
And yellow still
counters orange.

20
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.000
Every reply shown has
those same two-thirds odds.

21
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.267
That’s an advantage,

22
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.133
not a guaranteed win.

23
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:55.733
The advantages form a circle.

24
00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:57.967
There’s no best die
in this set

25
00:00:57.967 --> 00:00:59.367
just a better matchup.
